## Scope

This page adopts a classical charged complex scalar with a globally defined
real electromagnetic potential, so its field strength is exact. It states the
model's smoothness, SI units, arbitrary real coupling, scalar self-potential,
and compact variation conventions explicitly. Its local evolution result is a conditional deduction from the adopted action models and the current authored mathematical Cauchy theorem. The periodic branch retains integer $s\ge5$, complete finite-Sobolev charged data and compact admissibility. The general smooth branch uses the same explicit charged compatibility $\pi_i=\mathcal D_i\varphi_0$, with the spatial Levi-Civita derivative denoted separately. The mathematical comparison restores temporal matter gauge before reduced-system uniqueness and gives the stated isometry and global real gauge equivalence near the initial surface. No empirical, quantum, singular-source,
global-existence, or completeness claim is made.
